/-!
## Setting

We work in a unital C*-algebra `A` (the algebra of observables of a quantum spin system).
For a self-adjoint Hamiltonian `H` the Heisenberg dynamics is
`τ_t(a) = exp(i t H) * a * exp(-i t H)`.

The Lieb–Robinson bound asserts that if `a` and `b` are observables supported in
regions that are not coupled by the "free" part `H₀` of the Hamiltonian, then the
commutator `⁅τ_t(a), b⁆` stays small for small times: it is controlled by the strength
of the coupling term `V` times the elapsed time.  This is exactly the base case
(first order in `t`) of the Lieb–Robinson series which produces the exponential
light cone `e^{v|t| - d}`.
-/

namespace Frontier

open NormedSpace

variable {A : Type*} [CStarAlgebra A] [Nontrivial A]

noncomputable local instance ratAlg : NormedAlgebra ℚ A := .restrictScalars ℚ ℂ A

/-- The Heisenberg time evolution of the observable `a` generated by the Hamiltonian `H`:
`τ_t(a) = exp(i t H) * a * exp(-i t H)`. -/

theorem commute_conj_of_commute {X a b : A} (hXb : Commute X b) (hab : Commute a b) (t : ℝ) :
    ⁅exp (t • X) * a * exp (-(t • X)), b⁆ = 0 := by
  have h1 : Commute (exp (t • X)) b := ((hXb.smul_left t).exp_left)
  have h2 : Commute (exp (-(t • X))) b := (((hXb.smul_left t).neg_left).exp_left)
  have : Commute (exp (t • X) * a * exp (-(t • X))) b :=
    (h1.mul_left hab).mul_left h2
  rw [Ring.lie_def, this.eq, sub_self]

end Auxiliary

/-- **Lieb–Robinson bound (base case).**

Let `A` be a unital C*-algebra of observables, and let the Hamiltonian split as
`H = H₀ + V`, with `H₀` and `V` self-adjoint.  Let `a` and `b` be observables such that

* `a` and `b` commute (their supports are disjoint), and
* `H₀` commutes with `b` (the free part of the dynamics does not couple the region of
  `b` to that of `a`),

so that the only mechanism transporting information from `a` to `b` is the coupling
term `V`.  Then the Heisenberg-evolved observable `τ_t(a)` almost commutes with `b`,
with an error growing at most linearly in time:

`‖⁅τ_t(a), b⁆‖ ≤ 4 |t| ‖V‖ ‖a‖ ‖b‖`.

This is the effective light cone at first order: the commutator is negligible for
`|t| ≪ 1 / ‖V‖`, i.e. information propagates with a finite speed proportional to the
strength of the coupling. -/
